        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nate Albert, Rod Stewart, Brian Wilson\n- Companies: Capitol Records, Universal Music Group\n- Bands: The Mighty Mighty Bosstones\n- Albums: Back to the World\n- Roles: music executive, songwriter, producer, guitar player, Executive Vice President of A&R, rock singer\n\nFacts:\n- Brian Wilson signed with Capitol Records in 1962.\n- After signing with Capitol Records in 1962, Brian Wilson wrote or co-wrote more than two dozen Top 40 hits for his group.\n- Rod Stewart was born on 10 January 1945 and is a British rock singer and songwriter.\n- Nate Albert was born in 1970 and is an American music executive, songwriter, producer, and guitar player.\n- Nate Albert is the Executive Vice President of A&R at Capitol Records, which is a division of Universal Music Group.\n- Nate Albert formerly played in The Mighty Mighty Bosstones.\n- Nate Albert produced the album Back to the World.",
